+18. In the 02 series of amendments, the regulation is amended to account for vehicles equipped with an
+Automated Driving Systems (ADS2). Recognizing the need for different arrangements for vehicles fitted with
+ADS, this regulation has been amended to clarify that DCAS is only permitted to operate when a driver is in
+control, and that vehicles without the ability to be controlled by a driver (vehicles of Categories X and Y) are not
+required to comply with this regulation. These changes were introduced based on the assumption that ADS
+vehicles must have superior capabilities in executing the lateral and/or longitudinal control of the vehicle on a
+sustained basis during normal driving and when avoiding collision and/or mitigating the crash severity in critical
+situations. In the case of vehicles equipped with an ADS other than vehicles of Categories X and Y, in the manual
+driving mode no special provisions or exemptions apply.
